  "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a man with a stern expression and crossed arms, overlaid with text that reads, 'I hate everything about America. So I am going to move there to bring it Sharia law,' and at the bottom, 'the real reason for most Muslim immigration.' The visual and textual elements are juxtaposed to create a caricature of a Muslim individual as a threat to American values, implying that Muslims are inherently hostile and seek to impose Sharia law on the U.S. This is a clear example of Islamophobia, as it uses fearmongering about Sharia law to stigmatize and demonize Muslims. The meme's intent is to provoke fear and hostility toward Muslims by suggesting they are dangerous infiltrators who wish to impose their religious laws on a Western society, thereby promoting a hateful and discriminatory narrative. The overall intent is to incite prejudice and reinforce negative stereotypes about Muslims, which falls under the category of hateful content.",
